                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161112",
                        "subject": "Re: Alert for Weak Password switches to Reused Password when ignored",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T13:20:30.569-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-alert-for-weak-password-switches-to-reused-password-when-ignored/107875/replies/161112",
                        "body": "<P><a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" data-lia-user-mentions=\"\" data-lia-user-uid=\"22563\" data-lia-user-login=\"michelleh\" class=\"lia-mention lia-mention-user\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">michelleh\u200b</a>&nbsp;</P>\n<P>I'm sorry for the disruption. The issue being discussed in this thread is one where if you ignore a weak password alert Watchtower incorrectly displays a \"Reused Password\" banner for an item in \"Ignored Alerts\".</P>\n<P>Is this what your user is seeing? Or are they seeing the wrong type of banner being shown for an item that isn't in Ignored Alerts? Can you tell me a little more about the disruption this causes? Are you using 1Password Business and seeing incorrect data in the Business Watchtower report?&nbsp;</P>\n<P>-Dave</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161111",
                        "subject": "Re: Integration status: Connection Problem in Chrome on Win11",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T13:12:49.386-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password-work/re-integration-status-connection-problem-in-chrome-on-win11/159479/replies/161111",
                        "body": "<P>Thank you for sharing with the community!&nbsp;</P>\n<P>-Dave</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161110",
                        "subject": "Re: Feature request: Tag movement, clearing all memory.",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T13:04:06.230-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-feature-request-tag-movement-clearing-all-memory-/160869/replies/161110",
                        "body": "<P><a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" data-lia-user-mentions=\"\" data-lia-user-uid=\"22438\" data-lia-user-login=\"MeStesso\" class=\"lia-mention lia-mention-user\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">MeStesso\u200b</a>&nbsp;</P>\n<P>Thanks again for the feedback! Which features are implemented (and when) depends on a variety of factors that include: consideration for our existing product roadmap and planned features, urgent bug fixes that need to be prioritized over feature requests, available development resources, other customer feedback/requests, and more.&nbsp;</P>\n<P>All feedback is considered and prioritized carefully and the team works to implement features and fixes as quickly as possible.</P>\n<BLOCKQUOTE>\n<P>Empty all memory (including \"non-password\" fields) when the database is locked.</P>\n</BLOCKQUOTE>\n<P>Are you able to tell us a little more about this by sending an email to <A class=\"lia-external-url\" href=\"mailto:support@1Password.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">support@1Password.com</A> ? Our team would love to learn more about what information you're seeing in memory, how and when, after locking 1Password for Windows.&nbsp;</P>\n<P>-Dave</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161109",
                        "subject": "Don't miss tomorrow's Office Hours!",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T13:01:20.652-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/announcements/dont-miss-tomorrows-office-hours/161109",
                        "body": "<P>Hi 1Password Community!<BR /><BR />Would your team benefit from real-time help from 1Password experts? Join our <A href=\"https://events.zoom.us/eo/AvQ7ZKuVnJ5Zqp5Bj9xHnB96Wg33YVZRTZXFEA4kJZKZU0Sb9oKT~AggLXsr32QYFjq8BlYLZ5I06Dg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Office Hours for small and growing businesses</A> tomorrow at 8:30am EST.<BR /><BR />These casual, live sessions hosted by our Customer Success team are a great opportunity for customers on our <EM>Business</EM> or <EM>Teams</EM> plans to:</P><UL><LI>Ask questions and receive personalized guidance</LI><LI>Learn best practices on using the 1Password Browser Extension to make usage a breeze</LI><LI>Hear how others are leveraging 1Password to strengthen their security while making life easier</LI></UL><P>Bring your top-of-mind questions when you register; and we'll make sure you leave with the answers you need.<BR /><BR />We look forward to seeing you there!<BR /><BR />Register <A href=\"https://events.zoom.us/ev/AhgUs9uWulgcROPm42ddwv8PQt3IujF6RJnnW5AlyYtRjIOyksIL~AomZ-1ue0ar01AJJi11aQNaxZNYM7LKO3fDuGLmVdlk_wuYSz_9MTP5JcQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">here.</A></P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161108",
                        "subject": "Apple Watch does not appear in 1Password settings",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T12:52:33.505-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/apple-watch-does-not-appear-in-1password-settings/161108",
                        "body": "<P>This worked. But then I unpaired my watch and then reconnected it (checking on something unrelated). Since then I have not been able to unlock 1Password with my watch.&nbsp;</P><P>I can unlock my M1 MacMini (it has a secure enclave) with my watch.&nbsp;</P><UL><LI>I have restarted the watch</LI><LI>I have restarted the computer</LI><LI>I am running the latest Mac OS (18.6.2)</LI><LI>Bluetooth is enabled on the watch</LI></UL><P>What else should I try?</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161107",
                        "subject": "INCOMPATIBLE COMBINATIONS",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T12:51:08.204-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/incompatible-combinations/161107",
                        "body": "<P>I am generally satisfied with 1Password, though I have had a learning curve to overcome. However, it seems to me that certain combinations of browser, web site and 1Password just don't work.</P><P>Currently, I am not able to log in to Facebook and to my 55+ community's resident portal, nor can I change the password for either site.</P><P>I am using Firefox as my browser and have followed the instructions that are supposed to allow 1Password to operate properly with it.</P><P>Facebook itself provides absolutely no help. My 55+ community (managed by FirstService) had been trying to help me but the problem remains.</P><P>Has anyone else run into these kinds of problems? Are you able to use the Firefox browser with all web sites with 1Passport?</P><P>Can anyone help me with Facebook or do I just have to abandon my current Facebook account and start a new one?</P><P>Thank you in advance for any help!</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161106",
                        "subject": "Re: Autosubmit Feature Request: Also automatically tick \"Remember me\" / \"Keep me logged in\"",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T12:45:18.969-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-autosubmit-feature-request-also-automatically-tick-remember-me--keep-me-logge/115632/replies/161106",
                        "body": "<P><a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" data-lia-user-mentions=\"\" data-lia-user-uid=\"22604\" data-lia-user-login=\"TrishaM\" class=\"lia-mention lia-mention-user\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">TrishaM\u200b</a>&nbsp;</P>\n<P>I just tested MailChimp and it seems to be working for me with a new Login item:</P>\n<span class=\"lia-media-object lia-media-is-center\" data-image-alt=\"\"><button class=\"lia-media-unstyled-btn\" type=\"button\" aria-haspopup=\"true\" aria-label=\"Enlarge Image\"><img src=\"https://www.1password.community/t5/s/cuxzj43862/images/bS0xNjExMDYtSUVPNW5p?image-dimensions=203x240&amp;revision=1\" width=\"203\" height=\"240\" alt=\"\" /></button></span>\n<BLOCKQUOTE>\n<P>At the login screen I manually filled in my username and password and checked the \"keep me logged in\" box, then logged in and saved the (now) \"new\" item. &nbsp;&nbsp;</P>\n</BLOCKQUOTE>\n<P>It sounds like you used the auto-save prompt to save the login. You'll need to manually save the login after typing it in and before signing in by <STRONG>right-clicking</STRONG> on the page and then selecting <STRONG>1Password - Password Manager &gt; Save &gt; Login</STRONG>. Let me know if I misunderstood and you already tried that.&nbsp;</P>\n<P>-Dave</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161105",
                        "subject": "Re: Browser Extension Risk Clickjacking",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T12:41:18.192-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-browser-extension-risk-clickjacking/161087/replies/161105",
                        "body": "<P>Me, too! The spam, phishing attacks, and other account hacking seems to be getting worse and worse. If 1Password is vulnerable we are in big, big trouble.</P><P>Should we stop using the browser extension until 1Password announces a fix?</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161104",
                        "subject": "Re: Sorting order login items, etc.",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T12:11:09.612-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-sorting-order-login-items-etc-/159723/replies/161104",
                        "body": "<P><a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" data-lia-user-mentions=\"\" data-lia-user-uid=\"22317\" data-lia-user-login=\"seagull225\" class=\"lia-mention lia-mention-user\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">seagull225\u200b</a>&nbsp;</P>\n<P>The fix is now in the <A class=\"lia-external-url\" href=\"https://support.1password.com/betas/?mac\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">latest beta version</A> of 1Password (8.11.8-32 - released today) and hopefully will be released to the stable version soon. Thank you for your patience.&nbsp;</P>\n<P>-Dave</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161103",
                        "subject": "Re: Feature request: Previewing attached files on Apple Watch",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T12:00:19.303-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-feature-request-previewing-attached-files-on-apple-watch/161024/replies/161103",
                        "body": "<P>Hello! \ud83d\udc4b</P>\n<P>Thank you for the feature request! While I can't make any promises, I've filed this with our product team so that they can consider adding image viewing to the Apple Watch app in the future.&nbsp;</P>\n<P>For the time being, I recommend that you add whatever text you need as a <A class=\"lia-external-url\" href=\"https://support.1password.com/custom-fields/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">custom field</A> to the item in 1Password. Both iOS and macOS have a feature when you can copy text directly from the photo and then paste it into 1Password: <A class=\"lia-external-url\" href=\"https://support.apple.com/en-ca/120004\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Copy and translate text from photos on your iPhone or iPad</A></P>\n<P>I hope that helps.</P>\n<P>-Dave</P>\n<P><EM>PB-50359279</EM></P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161102",
                        "subject": "Re: 1Password shell plugins not working when configuration is stored in git",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T11:59:59.391-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/developers/re-1password-shell-plugins-not-working-when-configuration-is-stored-in-git/161029/replies/161102",
                        "body": "<P>Hi <a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" data-lia-user-mentions=\"\" data-lia-user-uid=\"13178\" data-lia-user-login=\"P4sca1\" class=\"lia-mention lia-mention-user\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">P4sca1\u200b</a> ,</P>\n<P>Let me feed this back to the team as feedback for evaluation.</P>\n<P>Thanks!<BR />Phil &amp; the Team</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161101",
                        "subject": "Re: flutter login example",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T11:57:45.957-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/developers/re-flutter-login-example/161044/replies/161101",
                        "body": "<P>Hi <a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" data-lia-user-mentions=\"\" data-lia-user-uid=\"10980\" data-lia-user-login=\"seankang\" class=\"lia-mention lia-mention-user\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">seankang\u200b</a>&nbsp;</P>\n<P>I'm not a Flutter developer but I came across the groupBy option.&nbsp; Have you tried using this when creating the form?</P>\n<P>I found this over on StackOverflow - https://stackoverflow.com/questions/68296566/flutter-how-to-groupby-two-or-more-fields</P>\n<P>Cheers,<BR />Phil</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161100",
                        "subject": "Re: Premature Completion",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T11:53:47.157-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/developers/re-premature-completion/161075/replies/161100",
                        "body": "<P>Hi <a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" data-lia-user-mentions=\"\" data-lia-user-uid=\"20761\" data-lia-user-login=\"captbackfire\" class=\"lia-mention lia-mention-user\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">captbackfire\u200b</a> ,</P>\n<P>Have you considered trying to do this with the SDKs? It might make editing the field a little more friendly. - <A class=\"lia-external-url\" href=\"https://developer.1password.com/docs/sdks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">https://developer.1password.com/docs/sdks</A>&nbsp;</P>\n<P>With the SDKs you can:<BR />1) Read out the full item to a variable<BR />2) Insert or update the needed fields<BR />3) Write it back into the vault<BR /><BR />Let me know if this works for you.</P>\n<P>Thanks,<BR />Phil</P>\n<P>&nbsp;</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161099",
                        "subject": "Re: Autosubmit Feature Request: Also automatically tick \"Remember me\" / \"Keep me logged in\"",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T11:42:17.396-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-autosubmit-feature-request-also-automatically-tick-remember-me--keep-me-logge/115632/replies/161099",
                        "body": "<P>Hi Dave,</P><P>Thank you for the very quick reply......unfortunately it does not work.&nbsp;<BR /><BR />One website I need to stay logged into all the time is MailChimp, where I spend a significant chunk of every workday.&nbsp;<BR /><BR />I deleted my MailChimp login entirely, even removing it from the 30-day sandbox for deleted items, and started over. &nbsp;At the login screen I manually filled in my username and password and checked the \"keep me logged in\" box, then logged in and saved the (now) \"new\" item. &nbsp;&nbsp;<BR /><BR />Then I logged out, and when I attempted to log back in, the \"keep me logged in\" box is not checked.&nbsp;<BR /><BR />I updated my version of 1Password on my Mac to the latest along with all my browsers and extensions, but no joy......it simply won't remember an auto-fill \"check\" for that field. &nbsp;:-(&nbsp;</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161098",
                        "subject": "Re: The macOS app crashes after every upgrade with Homebrew",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T11:41:07.837-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-the-macos-app-crashes-after-every-upgrade-with-homebrew/156299/replies/161098",
                        "body": "<P>Thank you for confirming!&nbsp;</P>\n<P>-Dave</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161097",
                        "subject": "Re: Browser Extension Risk Clickjacking",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T11:41:07.373-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-browser-extension-risk-clickjacking/161087/replies/161097",
                        "body": "<P>Where are we on this? I see there was a https://support.1password.com/browser-autofill-security/ yesterday, but are there any steps being taken to mitigate this vector in future updates? If so, when can we expect them?</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161096",
                        "subject": "Re: Autosubmit Feature Request: Also automatically tick \"Remember me\" / \"Keep me logged in\"",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T11:35:15.070-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-autosubmit-feature-request-also-automatically-tick-remember-me--keep-me-logge/115632/replies/161096",
                        "body": "<P><a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" data-lia-user-mentions=\"\" data-lia-user-uid=\"21467\" data-lia-user-login=\"rob-macindoe\" class=\"lia-mention lia-mention-user\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">rob-macindoe\u200b</a>&nbsp;</P>\n<P>I've filed your suggestion as a feature request on your behalf. \ud83d\ude42</P>\n<P>-Dave</P>\n<P><EM>PB-50357656</EM></P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161095",
                        "subject": "Re: Autosubmit Feature Request: Also automatically tick \"Remember me\" / \"Keep me logged in\"",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T11:33:41.378-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-autosubmit-feature-request-also-automatically-tick-remember-me--keep-me-logge/115632/replies/161095",
                        "body": "<P>Thank you for the suggestion, I've shared it with the team.&nbsp;</P>\n<P>-Dave</P>\n<P>PB-50357623</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161094",
                        "subject": "Re: Autosubmit Feature Request: Also automatically tick \"Remember me\" / \"Keep me logged in\"",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T11:30:52.580-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-autosubmit-feature-request-also-automatically-tick-remember-me--keep-me-logge/115632/replies/161094",
                        "body": "<P><a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" data-lia-user-mentions=\"\" data-lia-user-uid=\"22604\" data-lia-user-login=\"TrishaM\" class=\"lia-mention lia-mention-user\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">TrishaM\u200b</a>&nbsp;</P>\n<P>Welcome to the community! You can have 1Password remember to check the \"Remember Me\" box by saving a new login item using these steps:&nbsp;</P>\n<OL>\n<LI>Navigate to the website's login page.&nbsp;</LI>\n<LI>Type in your username and password manually but don't submit them yet.&nbsp;</LI>\n<LI>Check the \"Remember Me\" box.&nbsp;</LI>\n<LI>Right-click on the page and select <STRONG>1Password - Password Manager &gt; Save &gt; Login</STRONG>.&nbsp;</LI>\n<LI>Save a new login item, don't update the old one.&nbsp;</LI>\n</OL>\n<P><BR />Then try to fill the new login item. The Remember Me box should be automatically checked as well. If that doesn't work then can you share the name of a website where this doesn't work?</P>\n<P>-Dave</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161093",
                        "subject": "Re: Browser Extension Risk Clickjacking",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T11:26:48.026-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-browser-extension-risk-clickjacking/161087/replies/161093",
                        "body": "<P>Other details and demo:</P><UL><LI>https://marektoth.com/blog/dom-based-extension-clickjacking/</LI><LI>https://socket.dev/blog/password-manager-clickjacking/</LI></UL><UL><LI>https://websecurity.dev/password-managers/dom-based-extension-clickjacking/</LI></UL>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161092",
                        "subject": "Copy Button for Secure Notes in Browser Extension",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T11:25:20.914-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password-work/copy-button-for-secure-notes-in-browser-extension/161092",
                        "body": "<P>Hi team</P><P>Is it possible to request a feature that allows users to quickly copy the contents of a secure note directly from the browser extension? A simple icon or button to copy everything in a note would be very useful for those of us who need to access and paste secure information efficiently</P><P>Thanks for considering this</P><P>Best,<BR />Adam</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161091",
                        "subject": "Re: Android Search Bar Location",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T11:20:50.439-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-android-search-bar-location/159845/replies/161091",
                        "body": "<P><a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" data-lia-user-mentions=\"\" data-lia-user-uid=\"16527\" data-lia-user-login=\"casraf\" class=\"lia-mention lia-mention-user\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">casraf\u200b</a>&nbsp;</P>\n<P data-start=\"189\" data-end=\"438\">Thank you so much for sharing your feedback about search in 1Password for Android. We know how important it is to quickly find what you need, and we truly appreciate you taking the time to let us know what would make the experience better for you.</P>\n<P data-start=\"440\" data-end=\"724\">At the moment, based on the feedback we\u2019ve received from many customers across our different support channels, we don\u2019t have plans to change how search works right now. That said, our team is always exploring ways to make the app more helpful and intuitive, and your input plays a big role in guiding those improvements.</P>\n<P data-start=\"726\" data-end=\"866\">We\u2019re grateful for your perspective and the team will continue to iterate on the experience in future updates.</P>\n<P>-Dave</P>\n<P>PB-50357370</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161089",
                        "subject": "Re: New passwords saved in 1Password extension does not show up in app",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T10:39:37.271-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-new-passwords-saved-in-1password-extension-does-not-show-up-in-app/161088/replies/161089",
                        "body": "<P>I was editing another login in the 1P app. After saving that edit, the new entry for Wikimedia finally did show up. This was probably 5-10 minutes after first creating the new login using the extension (in Brave).</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161088",
                        "subject": "New passwords saved in 1Password extension does not show up in app",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T10:33:23.985-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/new-passwords-saved-in-1password-extension-does-not-show-up-in-app/161088",
                        "body": "<P>I just created a new password for Wikipedia, which uses auth.wikimedia.org. It shows up fine in the 1Password extension and can be used from there.</P><P>Normally I expect to see the new password also recorded in the 1Password app. However, it is not there.</P><P>Further, it cannot be edited in the extension either. In the extension, it only has a password, but no username.</P><P>Odd behavior.</P><P>&nbsp;</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161087",
                        "subject": "Browser Extension Risk Clickjacking",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T10:27:50.990-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/browser-extension-risk-clickjacking/161087",
                        "body": "<P>According to this report, I wondered what the position of 1Password is on this issue and when it will be fixed.</P><P><A class=\"lia-external-url\" href=\"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/major-password-managers-can-leak-logins-in-clickjacking-attacks/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/major-password-managers-can-leak-logins-in-clickjacking-attacks/</A></P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161086",
                        "subject": "Re: Autosubmit Feature Request: Also automatically tick \"Remember me\" / \"Keep me logged in\"",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T09:52:24.910-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-autosubmit-feature-request-also-automatically-tick-remember-me--keep-me-logge/115632/replies/161086",
                        "body": "<P>Could someone on the Dev team post an update on this feature to save and auto-fill(check) the \"remember me\" checkbox? &nbsp;<BR /><BR />My 1Password browser extensions&nbsp;<EM>were</EM> previously saving and auto-checking the \"remember me\" or \"keep me logged in\" boxes but that seems to have been removed, it no longer does that and won't save it no matter what I do (I'm on the most current version as of today, 8.11.6). &nbsp;When I view those logins in either a browser extension or the desktop app, that field is no longer part of the record.<BR /><BR />This is a vital need for me and nothing I've tried (\"updating\" logins after checking that field, deleting and recreating/saving logins with it checked, trying to manually add it as a text field)....</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161085",
                        "subject": "Re: Brave browser, autofill & Brave shields",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T09:45:54.476-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-brave-browser-autofill--brave-shields/161074/replies/161085",
                        "body": "<P>Hi Dave,&nbsp; &nbsp;So far chewy.com and caremark.com were giving me issues until I turned off the Brave shield.&nbsp; &nbsp;I haven't added any other filters .&nbsp; I'll reply here if or when I come across any other websites.</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161084",
                        "subject": "Re: Any experience of 1Password with Safari 26 (beta) yet?",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T09:03:51.145-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-any-experience-of-1password-with-safari-26-beta-yet/161025/replies/161084",
                        "body": "<P>Hello <a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" data-lia-user-mentions=\"\" data-lia-user-uid=\"15242\" data-lia-user-login=\"ChrisJenkins\" class=\"lia-mention lia-mention-user\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">ChrisJenkins\u200b</a>! \ud83d\udc4b</P>\n<P>Thanks for the question! Our team is testing 1Password with macOS Tahoe and the beta version of Safari. As with any beta, there are a few different issues currently being tracked, the most notable being an issue where 1Password's icon in a username/password may disappear in certain situations after being clicked. You can workaround that issue by filling from the pop-up.</P>\n<P>If you do decide to test masOS Tahoe and run into issues then let me know and I'll get them filed for our development team. I'd also be interested to hear the experiences of other members of the community who might already be running macOS Tahoe.&nbsp;</P>\n<P>-Dave</P>\n<P><EM>#38808</EM></P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161083",
                        "subject": "Re: Brave browser, autofill & Brave shields",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T08:54:10.344-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-brave-browser-autofill--brave-shields/161074/replies/161083",
                        "body": "<P>Hello <a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" data-lia-user-mentions=\"\" data-lia-user-uid=\"22597\" data-lia-user-login=\"AerospaceEd\" class=\"lia-mention lia-mention-user\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">AerospaceEd\u200b</a>! \ud83d\udc4b</P>\n<P>Thank you for sharing your workaround! It sounds like there's some sort of filter that is interfering with 1Password. Out of curiosity, have you enabled or added any other filters from the default ones here: <STRONG>brave://settings/shields/filters</STRONG></P>\n<P>And are you able to share any of the websites that you've run into issues on?&nbsp;</P>\n<P>-Dave</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161082",
                        "subject": "Re: [Bug report] Item fields reordering issue",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T08:20:54.260-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-bug-report-item-fields-reordering-issue/97542/replies/161082",
                        "body": "<P>Hi everyone,<BR /><BR />I'm happy to share that this bug has been fixed in version 8.11.6. Please let us know if you're still observing it after updating!</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161081",
                        "subject": "Re: Disable \"sign in with passkey\" popup",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T08:12:58.698-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-disable-sign-in-with-passkey-popup/161053/replies/161081",
                        "body": "<P><a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" data-lia-user-mentions=\"\" data-lia-user-uid=\"9183\" data-lia-user-login=\"KazuT\" class=\"lia-mention lia-mention-user\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">KazuT\u200b</a>&nbsp;</P>\n<P>Thank you for the reply. It looks like your screenshot shows a \"Save login\" prompt (for passwords) and not a passkey prompt like your first post mentioned. If this is the prompt that you're seeing then you can turn it off if you wish:&nbsp;</P>\n<OL>\n<LI>Open your browser.</LI>\n<LI>Right-click on the 1Password icon in your browser's toolbar and click <STRONG>Settings</STRONG>.</LI>\n<LI>Turn off \"Offer to save logins\".</LI>\n</OL>\n<P><BR />I hope that helps.&nbsp;</P>\n<P>-Dave</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161080",
                        "subject": "Re: 1Password Chrome Extension on Mac has problematic login",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T08:02:16.207-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-1password-chrome-extension-on-mac-has-problematic-login/160937/replies/161080",
                        "body": "<P><a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" data-lia-user-mentions=\"\" data-lia-user-uid=\"6729\" data-lia-user-login=\"komocode\" class=\"lia-mention lia-mention-user\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">komocode\u200b</a>&nbsp;</P>\n<P>Thank you for the feedback. Currently, the menu bar icon is required in order for the 1Password desktop app to run in the background even when the main window is closed. This is so that 1Password is never running and unlocked on your Mac without you being aware of it.&nbsp;</P>\n<P>Without the menu bar icon being visible, the 1Password desktop app will completely close once you close the main window. Since the desktop app handles Touch ID, the browser extension will need to wait for it to open back up before it can present the Touch ID prompt. This is likely why you were seeing the password prompt appear first.&nbsp;</P>\n<P>That being said, I've shared your feedback with our product team internally.&nbsp;</P>\n<P>-Dave</P>\n<P><EM>PB-50354143</EM></P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161079",
                        "subject": "Central Control for Autofill Exclusions in 1Password Business",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T07:54:07.446-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password-work/central-control-for-autofill-exclusions-in-1password-business/161079",
                        "body": "<P>It would be very helpful if administrators in 1Password Business could set a policy to disable autofill for specific domains or subdomains. For internal portals like Topdesk we don\u2019t need login items, and autofill only gets in the way.&nbsp;As an admin, I\u2019d like to be able to centrally push this setting to a group, so users don\u2019t have to configure it themselves. This would remove frustration for our team and make management much easier.</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161078",
                        "subject": "Re: Mac App Store??",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T07:32:05.857-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-mac-app-store/161018/replies/161078",
                        "body": "<P><a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" data-lia-user-mentions=\"\" data-lia-user-uid=\"14465\" data-lia-user-login=\"noraar\" class=\"lia-mention lia-mention-user\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">noraar\u200b</a>&nbsp;</P>\n<P>I don't have any plans to share at this time. We're currently rolling out updates to the web app at 1Password.com to have it more closely align with the desktop app in terms of user experience and performance. The web app, along with 1Password for Safari from the Mac App Store, might be a solution for some of your users.&nbsp;</P>\n<P>If you haven't already, you can sign-up to be notified if there's any news about the Mac App Store in the future: <A class=\"lia-external-url\" href=\"https://1password.com/mac-app-store-subscribe/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow noreferrer\">https://1password.com/mac-app-store-subscribe/</A></P>\n<P>-Dave</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161077",
                        "subject": "Re: Offline error",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T07:24:30.343-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/re-offline-error/161019/replies/161077",
                        "body": "<P><a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" data-lia-user-mentions=\"\" data-lia-user-uid=\"22438\" data-lia-user-login=\"MeStesso\" class=\"lia-mention lia-mention-user\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">MeStesso\u200b</a>&nbsp;</P>\n<P>Thank you for the reply. So that I can look into this further, and find a solution,&nbsp;I'd like to ask you to create and share a 1Password diagnostics report from your Windows PC:<BR /><BR /><A href=\"https://support.1password.com/diagnostics/?windows\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"><STRONG>Send a diagnostics report (Windows)</STRONG></A><BR /><BR />Attach the diagnostics to an email message addressed to <STRONG>support@1password.com</STRONG><BR /><BR />With your email please include:</P>\n<UL>\n<LI>A link to this thread: <EM>https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/offline-error/161019</EM></LI>\n<LI>Your forum username: <EM>MeStesso</EM></LI>\n</UL>\n<P><BR />You should receive an automated reply from our BitBot assistant with a Support ID number.&nbsp; <STRONG>Please post that number here.</STRONG>&nbsp; Thanks very much!</P>\n<P>-Dave</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161076",
                        "subject": "Re: Premature Completion",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T06:55:20.724-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/developers/re-premature-completion/161075/replies/161076",
                        "body": "<P>Credit where credit is due: the realization^ that I could tell 1P not to automatically login came from <a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" data-lia-user-mentions=\"\" data-lia-user-uid=\"28\" data-lia-user-login=\"1P_Timothy\" class=\"lia-mention lia-mention-user\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">1P_Timothy\u200b</a>'s comment <A class=\"lia-internal-link lia-internal-url lia-internal-url-content-type-forum\" href=\"https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/premature-completion/156837/replies/156961\" target=\"_blank\" data-lia-auto-title=\"here\" data-lia-auto-title-active=\"0\">here</A>. But, that isn't the solution I'm looking for.</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161075",
                        "subject": "Premature Completion",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T06:19:28.006-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/developers/premature-completion/161075",
                        "body": "<P>(moving <A class=\"lia-internal-link lia-internal-url lia-internal-url-content-type-forum\" href=\"https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/premature-completion/156837\" data-lia-auto-title=\"this discussion\" data-lia-auto-title-active=\"0\" target=\"_blank\">this discussion</A> from Community Forum because this may be more in scope here)</P><P>I use a Microsoft 365 account, both personally and for work. I am having a terrible time with the authentication flow because 1Password automatically inputs the code for me in the interstitial screen (a benefit, to be sure), but its haste doesn't check, or allow me to check, the box that says \"Don't ask again for 30 days\". Checking this box is the only way to get the Microsoft KMSI to work when I have multiple profile browser windows open. Is there a way to have 1Password check this box for me by default (i.e., a boolean field that knows the ID or class of the checkbox)?</P><P>I realize I can tell 1P not to login automatically, but it looks like there should be another way to accomplish this through the CLI...</P><P>I've looked through the developer documentation, and I cannot see a type for checkbox. I looked at the JSON for my login to this community site, and it lists some form fields I filled out when signing up that had checkboxes listed as strings with checkmark characters for the value:</P><pre class=\"lia-code-sample language-json\"><code>{\n \"id\": \"\",\n \"type\": \"STRING\",\n \"label\": \"custom.roleDeveloper\",\n \"value\": \"\u2713\",\n \"reference\": \"op://Private/1Password Support Community/custom.roleDeveloper\" \n}</code></pre><P>I got this using the CLI:</P><pre class=\"lia-code-sample language-bash\"><code>op item get \"1Password Support Community\" --format json &gt; opcomm.json</code></pre><P>op item get \"1Password Support Community\" --format json &gt; opcomm.json</P><P>However, the schema for this JSON is different than the Copy item JSON menu option from the interface:</P><pre class=\"lia-code-sample language-json\"><code>{\n \"value\": \"\u2713\",\n \"id\": \"RegistrationForm-custom.roleDeveloper\",\n \"name\": \"custom.roleDeveloper\",\n \"type\": \"C\" \n}</code></pre><P>^ THIS is the JSON I want to be able to modify, and specifically add a new field to. Here's why...</P><P>When I export this JSON from my M365 entry, there's an extra little thing that acts like a tab order:</P><pre class=\"lia-code-sample language-json\"><code>{\n \"value\": \"Sign in\",\n \"name\": \"\",\n \"type\": \"I\",\n \"id\": \"idSIButton9;opid=__11\" \n}</code></pre><P>That \"opid=\", as best I can tell, sets an order of interaction with the form fields in the interface. I want to be able to add something like this (all field values taken from online sources and DOM inspection):</P><pre class=\"lia-code-sample language-json\"><code>{\n \"value\": \"\u2713\",\n \"name\": \"rememberMFA\",\n \"type\": \"C\",\n \"id\": \"idChkBx_SAOTCC_TD;opid=__17\" \n}</code></pre><P>The Catch 22 is: I don't see any way to do this.</P><P>Any ideas would be appreciated.</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:160849",
                        "subject": "Identity theft",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T06:11:47.426-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/kb/cybersecurity-glossary/identity-theft/160849",
                        "body": "<P>Identity theft is a serious crime that can affect anyone.</P>\n<P>Attackers can use a victim\u2019s identity to try to steal money, take over online accounts, or commit crimes in the victim's name. As more aspects of daily life move online, the risk of your personal information landing in the wrong hands increases. This makes it all the more important to know how to protect the various aspects of your identity from being used in unauthorized ways.</P>\n<P>But there's a lot you can do to minimize the threat and impact of identity theft. In this article, you\u2019ll learn what identity theft is, how to avoid it, what you should do if you\u2019re targeted, and how password managers like 1Password can help keep you safe online.&nbsp;</P>\n<H4 id=\"community-160849-toc-hId-1228473936\">What is identity theft?</H4>\n<P>Identity theft refers to any activity in which someone uses your personal or financial information without your permission. This can include details like your name, Social Insurance Number, driver\u2019s license, or credit card number.&nbsp;</P>\n<P>Criminals often use identity theft for some type of financial benefit, such as:</P>\n<UL>\n<LI aria-level=\"1\">Accessing the targeted person\u2019s bank account,</LI>\n<LI aria-level=\"1\">Fraudulently signing up for a new credit card or taking out a bank loan,</LI>\n<LI aria-level=\"1\">Filing a false government tax return,</LI>\n<LI aria-level=\"1\">Pursuing other benefits, like filling a medical prescription or traveling under another person\u2019s name.</LI>\n</UL>\n<H4 id=\"community-160849-toc-hId--1323683025\">How does identity theft occur?</H4>\n<P>How a thief gains access to personal information can vary.</P>\n<P>For example, the thief could steal the targeted person\u2019s financial information without their knowledge by attaching a credit card skimmer to an ATM. They can trick the target into sharing personal information by calling the target and pretending to be a bank employee. (This is also known as \u201c<A href=\"https://blog.1password.com/what-is-social-engineering-hacking-101/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow noreferrer\">social engineering</A>\u201d.) They could even gain access to accounts that store the target\u2019s personal information, such as taking advantage of a data breach to obtain sign-in credentials.</P>\n<H4 id=\"community-160849-toc-hId-419127310\">Why is it important to keep an eye out for identity theft?</H4>\n<P>While the chances of being affected by identity theft are relatively low, it's important to take the threat seriously, as the consequences can be severe and long-lasting. One of the biggest impacts is the financial loss that can occur. This can lead to the victim losing substantial amounts of money \u2013 even their life savings \u2013 which can be burdensome or sometimes impossible to restore.</P>\n<P>Credit score damage is another common consequence of identity theft. Excessive spending on a credit card can result in a credit card bill that\u2019s challenging to repay, especially if the credit card company can\u2019t or won\u2019t reverse the charges. You may not even realize a new credit card is in your name until you notice a decrease in your credit score. It can then be difficult to get a bank loan, mortgage, and other credit approvals if your score has been damaged in this way.</P>\n<P>Beyond your savings and credit score, identity theft can lead to additional stressors like your accounts being flagged or inaccessible, unexpected legal fees, and the emotional distress that comes with someone stealing your identity.</P>\n<P>While the repercussions can be serious, you shouldn't lose hope. There are plenty of ways to protect yourself and minimize the likelihood of being someone's next victim.</P>\n<H4 id=\"community-160849-toc-hId--2133029651\">What are the indicators of identity theft and how should you respond?</H4>\n<P>Here are some telltale signs of identity theft to keep an eye out for:</P>\n<UL>\n<LI aria-level=\"1\">Unauthorized transactions in your bank accounts or credit cards.&nbsp;</LI>\n<LI aria-level=\"1\">Unexpected changes to your credit score or report.</LI>\n<LI aria-level=\"1\">Mail or bills in your name that you didn\u2019t sign up for.</LI>\n<LI aria-level=\"1\">Data breaches that could include your personal information.</LI>\n</UL>\n<P>If you suspect you\u2019ve been the target of identity theft, the most important step is to tell someone. It can feel embarrassing to realize someone has stolen your information, but it\u2019s important to act fast. This can include reporting the suspicious activity \u2013 such as calling your bank, credit card company, and/or local authorities. If your credit score may be affected, you can also report the theft to a credit reporting agency. And be sure to freeze any accounts in question to prevent any further unauthorized access or spending.</P>\n<H4 id=\"community-160849-toc-hId--390219316\">How can 1Password help you defend against identity theft?</H4>\n<P>The most effective way to protect yourself from identity theft is to prevent others from accessing your personal information to begin with.&nbsp;</P>\n<P>You can use a password manager like 1Password to securely store your account credentials and other private information, making it much harder for anyone else to gain access. 1Password is especially effective thanks to its <A href=\"https://support.1password.com/1password-security/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow noreferrer\">unique security design</A>. To make your passwords stronger and more unique, use <A href=\"https://1password.com/password-generator\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow noreferrer\">1Password\u2019s built-in password generator</A>. This will help prevent unpermitted access, even by <A href=\"https://blog.1password.com/what-is-a-brute-force-attack-and-whats-the-best-defense/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow noreferrer\">brute force attacks</A>.&nbsp;</P>\n<P>1Password\u2019s <A href=\"https://watchtower.1password.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow noreferrer\">Watchtower</A> is also a useful tool for protecting yourself from identity theft. It will alert you to data breaches that involve your information and other security issues, allowing you to respond faster if your accounts have been compromised. In addition, Watchtower can help you avoid identity theft in the future by flagging weak passwords and online accounts that support 2FA or passkeys.&nbsp;</P>\n<P>Need to share an item from your 1Password account? Send a secure link using our <A href=\"https://support.1password.com/share-items\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow noreferrer\">item sharing</A> feature. Every link is a \"snapshot\" of the item in your 1Password account. So, if you change the item after you've sent the link \u2013 such as updating the password \u2013 your recipient won't have access to the new version. It also allows you to specify who can view the item and to set an expiration on the link.&nbsp;</P>\n<P>Beyond the tools you use to keep your personal information safe, it\u2019s important to stay alert and be cautious of any suspicious activity. Turn on notifications for credit and banking charges, read your emails from your bank and government accounts, avoid sharing personal information unless absolutely required, and put on your detective hat if something doesn\u2019t seem right with your credit score. Some preventative action now can save you from a big headache in the future.</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161074",
                        "subject": "Brave browser, autofill & Brave shields",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T04:21:59.329-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password/brave-browser-autofill--brave-shields/161074",
                        "body": "<P>I started to use the Brave browser on my desktop&nbsp; computer and noticed with a few websites I wasn't getting the 1password login dropdown, either automatically or by clicking the 1password icon in the login field. I have the browser extension and desktop app installed.&nbsp; If I click on autofill from the extension it works as expected.&nbsp; &nbsp;I found this solution: The Brave browser has an option called Brave shields, when I turn this off for the website in question then the login dropdown appears.</P><P>&nbsp;</P>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
                        "id": "message:161073",
                        "subject": "Re: Integration status: Connection Problem in Chrome on Win11",
                        "postTime": "2025-08-20T04:17:39.620-07:00",
                        "viewHref": "https://www.1password.community/discussions/1password-work/re-integration-status-connection-problem-in-chrome-on-win11/159479/replies/161073",
                        "body": "<P>Thank you very much for analyzing my policy settings. Finally, the solution was found:<BR /><BR /></P><BLOCKQUOTE><P>you will need to ... set com.1password.1password as an exception to the NativeMessagingAllowlist policy for the NativeMessaging process to get the integration working again...</P></BLOCKQUOTE>",
                        "author": {
                            "title": null,
                            "lastName": null,
                            "firstName": null
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "node": {
